; FBX 7.7.0 project file
; ----------------------------------------------------
; SYNTHETIC (batch R). Not produced by any DCC tool.
;
; WHY: `data/*.fbx` (690 files) contains no node whose RotationPivot falls strictly inside
; (0, 0.0009765625), and no node with 0 < |rp-sp|_1 <= 0.001. Both are load-bearing:
;   * `ufbxi_is_vec3_zero()` (ufbx.c:11570) is EXACT (== 0.0) and gates
;     UFBX_PIVOT_HANDLING_ADJUST_TO_PIVOT;
;   * `ufbxi_pivot_nonzero()` (ufbx.c:18091) uses |x| >= 0.0009765625 and gates
;     UFBX_PIVOT_HANDLING_ADJUST_TO_ROTATION_PIVOT (over rp / sp / so).
; A RotationPivot of 0.0005 makes the two disagree -- ADJUST_TO_PIVOT engages,
; ADJUST_TO_ROTATION_PIVOT does not -- which is exactly the discrimination the real corpus
; cannot produce.
;
;   * The same node has |rp - sp|_1 = 0.0005, i.e. 0 < err <= pivot_epsilon(0.001)
;     (ufbx.c:18370-18376), so `can_modify_pivot` stays TRUE. That is the boundary the real
;     corpus never reaches (measured: the smallest non-zero pivot component anywhere in
;     data/ is 0.00799 -- 8x the `ufbxi_pivot_nonzero` threshold).

FBXHeaderExtension:  {
	FBXHeaderVersion: 1004
	FBXVersion: 7700
	Creator: "ufbx-cs batch R synthetic"
}
